{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And the children of Israel journeyed and encamped in Oboth.</b> They said in the Midrash: they became enemies (oyevim) to the Place — a play on the name Oboth. And they encamped in Iyei-ha-Avarim, which were full of wrath (avrah). And they encamped in the valley of Zered — the valley was nothing but full of roaring flood (zered), and they could not cross it for 38 years; this is what is written (Deuteronomy 2:14): ״ועברו לכם את נחל זרד״, and it is written (ibid.): ״והימים אשר הלכנו מקדש ברנע עד אשר עברנו את נחל זרד שלשים ושמנה שנה״. From there they journeyed and encamped beyond Arnon, for the Holy One, blessed be He, was reconciled to them — thus far. And it appears proper to say that the statement 'the Holy One, blessed be He, was reconciled to them' refers to what is said 'beyond Arnon' — for it should have said 'they encamped at the crossing of Arnon,' but it said 'beyond,' because that wrath which had rested upon them all 38 years, during which they were rebuked, had departed from them; therefore it says that the Holy One, blessed be He, was reconciled to them. And likewise we find that immediately the divine speech came to Moses and the Holy One, blessed be He, said to him at once (ibid.): ״קומו סעו ועברו את נחל ארנון״, in the manner of what is written in Deuteronomy."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:34:34.309023601Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}